<article class="env-lemma" id="0FZ2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FZ2">Lemma <span data-tag="0FZ2">57.9.3</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian ring. Let $X$ be a separated finite type scheme over $R$ which has the resolution property. Set $\mathcal{O}_\Delta = \Delta _*(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ where $\Delta : X \to X \times _ R X$ is the diagonal of $X/k$. There exists a resolution </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \ldots \to \mathcal{E}_2 \boxtimes \mathcal{G}_2 \to \mathcal{E}_1 \boxtimes \mathcal{G}_1 \to \mathcal{E}_0 \boxtimes \mathcal{G}_0 \to \mathcal{O}_\Delta \to 0  \]
</div>
  <p> where each $\mathcal{E}_ i$ and $\mathcal{G}_ i$ is a finite locally free $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $X$ is separated, the diagonal morphism $\Delta $ is a closed immersion and hence $\mathcal{O}_\Delta $ is a coherent $\mathcal{O}_{X \times _ R X}$-module (Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/087T" data-tag="087T">30.9.8</a>). Thus the lemma follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/0FZ0" data-tag="0FZ0">57.9.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>